<title>RUSSIA: Rouble eases after earlier central bank selling.</title>
<headline>Rouble eases after earlier central bank selling.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The rouble eased ahead of the weekend after active central bank rouble selling earlier this week, dealers said on Friday.</p>
<p> roubles/dollar	Mar 14 midday  Mar 14 early   Mar 13 close</p>
<p> today settlement    5,706-08	 5,706-08	 5,696-98</p>
<p> tomorrow settlement 5,706-07	 5,707-09	 5,705-07</p>
<p> overnight credit (%)    5-10	     5-15	     5-15</p>
<p>			   Mar 14				Mar 13</p>
<p> central bank	  5,695/5,711			 5,692/5,708</p>
<p> MICEX		   5,703				 5,701</p>
<p>&quot;The market paused for breath, as usual on Friday. Roubles have become cheap after constant dollar selling to the central bank,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Dealers said some roubles could be also coming from the Treasury bill market.</p>
<p>--Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
</text>
